  "articleBody": "Getting a roof estimate isn't just about the bottom line price; it's about understanding exactly what you're paying for and making sure you're getting a quality job that protects your home for years. Knowing the right questions to ask during your consultation can help you compare bids effectively and feel confident in your choice.\n\nQuestions to Ask Before You Decide:\n- What specific materials and manufacturer/product line will be used? Don't just settle for 'shingles.' Ask about the brand, type, and specific product line to ensure quality and compatibility with Texas weather.\n- Will the existing roof be removed, or are you proposing an overlay? It's crucial to know if they're tearing off the old roof. Removing it allows for inspection of the decking and often leads to a more durable installation.\n- How will damaged decking be priced and handled? Find out if there's an allowance for unforeseen decking damage once the old roof is off, and what the per-sheet cost would be if extra work is needed.\n- What ventilation and flashing work is included in the estimate? Proper ventilation and flashing are essential for preventing leaks and extending roof life. Make sure these critical components are clearly itemized.\n- Who is responsible for obtaining necessary permits, and how will waste be handled? Permits are often required for re-roofing, and you'll want to know if the contractor manages this. Also, confirm how debris will be removed and if cleanup is included.\n- What warranties cover the materials and the workmanship? Understand the length and terms of both the manufacturer's warranty on the materials and the contractor's warranty on their labor.\n- Can you provide proof of workers’ compensation and general liability insurance? This is incredibly important. If a worker gets injured on your property or there's accidental damage, you want to be sure the contractor is properly insured, protecting you from potential liability.\n\nAsking these questions helps you peel back the layers of a quote and compare 'apples to apples' between different contractors. We're committed to transparent communication and giving you all the details.\n\nWhat to Do Next:\nPrepare these questions for your roof estimate consultation. Discounted Roofing Co. is ready to provide a detailed, clear estimate.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}